from common import save
H = [
("What were the ancient civilizations?","Major ancient civilizations: Mesopotamia (Sumer, between the Tigris and Euphrates, invented writing ~3200 BCE), Egypt (Nile, pyramids), Indus Valley (Harappa, Mohenjo-daro), China (Yellow River), Greece, Rome, and the Maya, Aztec and Inca in the Americas.",["ancient civilizations","oldest civilization","mesopotamia","early civilizations"]),
("Who built the pyramids?","The ancient Egyptians built the pyramids as tombs for pharaohs. The Great Pyramid of Giza was built for Pharaoh Khufu around 2560 BCE and was the tallest human-made structure for about 3,800 years.",["pyramids of egypt","great pyramid of giza","who made the pyramids"]),
("What was the Roman Empire?","The Roman Empire ruled the Mediterranean and much of Europe from 27 BCE (Augustus, the first emperor) until the West fell in 476 CE; the Eastern (Byzantine) Empire lasted until 1453. Rome gave us Latin, laws, roads, aqueducts and the calendar.",["roman empire","fall of rome","julius caesar","augustus"]),
("Who was Alexander the Great?","Alexander the Great (356–323 BCE), king of Macedonia and a student of Aristotle, built an empire from Greece to north-west India, defeating Porus at the Battle of the Hydaspes (Jhelum) in 326 BCE.",["alexander the great","alexander and porus"]),
("What was the Renaissance?","The Renaissance ('rebirth') was a revival of art, science and learning in Europe from the 14th to 17th centuries, starting in Italy. Famous figures: Leonardo da Vinci, Michelangelo, Raphael and Galileo.",["renaissance","european renaissance"]),
("What was the Cold War?","The Cold War (1947–1991) was a long rivalry between the USA and the Soviet Union, fought through an arms race, the space race and proxy wars rather than direct war. It ended when the Soviet Union broke up in 1991.",["cold war","ussr breakup","soviet union"]),
("What was the space race?","The space race was the USA–USSR competition in space: the USSR launched Sputnik 1 (1957, the first satellite) and Yuri Gagarin (1961, the first human in space); the USA landed Apollo 11 on the Moon (1969).",["space race","sputnik","first satellite"]),
("What was the Partition of India?","In August 1947, British India was divided into India and Pakistan (including East Pakistan, which became Bangladesh in 1971). Millions of people were displaced and many died in the violence. The border was drawn by Cyril Radcliffe.",["partition of india","india pakistan partition","radcliffe line","bangladesh independence"]),
("What was the Battle of Plassey?","In the Battle of Plassey (1757), Robert Clive's East India Company forces defeated Siraj-ud-Daulah, the Nawab of Bengal, beginning British control of India. The Battle of Buxar (1764) strengthened it.",["battle of plassey","battle of buxar","east india company"]),
("What were the battles of Panipat?","Three battles of Panipat: the First (1526), Babur defeated Ibrahim Lodi and founded the Mughal Empire; the Second (1556), Akbar's forces defeated Hemu; the Third (1761), Ahmad Shah Abdali defeated the Marathas.",["battles of panipat","second battle of panipat","third battle of panipat"]),
("Who was Tipu Sultan?","Tipu Sultan (1751–1799), the 'Tiger of Mysore', ruled the Kingdom of Mysore and fought the British East India Company, using early iron-cased rockets. He died defending Srirangapatna in 1799.",["tipu sultan","tiger of mysore","anglo mysore wars"]),
("Who was Veerapandiya Kattabomman?","Veerapandiya Kattabomman was a Palayakarar (chieftain) of Panchalankurichi in Tamil Nadu who refused to pay taxes to the British East India Company; he was hanged in 1799 and is remembered as an early freedom fighter.",["kattabomman","veerapandiya kattabomman","panchalankurichi"]),
("Who was Velu Nachiyar?","Velu Nachiyar (1730–1796), queen of Sivaganga, was the first Indian queen to fight and defeat the British East India Company, winning back her kingdom in 1780. She is called 'Veeramangai'.",["velu nachiyar","veeramangai","queen of sivaganga"]),
("What was the Vellore Mutiny?","The Vellore Mutiny of 10 July 1806 was a revolt by Indian soldiers against the British at Vellore Fort, Tamil Nadu — over 50 years before the 1857 revolt.",["vellore mutiny","vellore revolt 1806"]),
("What was the Salt Satyagraha in Tamil Nadu?","In 1930, C. Rajagopalachari (Rajaji) led a salt march from Tiruchirappalli to Vedaranyam, breaking the salt law alongside Gandhi's Dandi March.",["vedaranyam salt march","rajaji salt satyagraha"]),
("Who was C. Rajagopalachari?","C. Rajagopalachari (Rajaji, 1878–1972) was a freedom fighter, the last Governor-General of India (1948–1950) and the only Indian to hold that post, and Chief Minister of Madras. He received the first Bharat Ratna in 1954.",["rajaji","c rajagopalachari","last governor general of india","first indian governor general"]),
("What was the Industrial Revolution's effect?","The Industrial Revolution moved work from farms and home crafts to factories and cities, brought railways and steam power, raised production enormously, and also caused pollution and harsh working conditions, leading to labour laws.",["effects of industrial revolution"]),
("What was the Green Revolution?","The Green Revolution (1960s–70s) used high-yield seeds, irrigation and fertilisers to boost food production. In India it was led by M. S. Swaminathan, mainly for wheat and rice in Punjab, Haryana and western Uttar Pradesh, making India self-sufficient in grain.",["green revolution india","father of green revolution"]),
]
